Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 19:44:25 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 083/154] feat(commandbar): build action rows from the hotkey
 registry
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The page owned a literal list of seven verbs, so a row and the key that
runs it could drift apart and no row could show its binding. The rows
come from the hotkey table now, pushed once per open, each carrying the
combo it is bound to. A rebinding is in force by the next open, which is
when the chip follows it. Two letters is the shortest query that offers
a verb, or one letter buries the omnibox rows under the whole catalog.

The build file hunks interleave, so this also carries the URL and net
dependencies the hygiene pass needs, the target for the shared scorer,
and a reordering of entries that belongs to neither.

Signed-off-by: János Mikó <693558+janosmiko@users.noreply.github.com>
